  "boundary_notes": [
    "This foundation slice implements configuration, matrix-fed CBVs, explicit HDR/tone-map separation and graph scheduling preparation. CSM/local shadows, TAA/history, automatic exposure, Bloom, SSR, froxel volumes and transparency retain subsequent M4.3 work.",
    "The current backend still submits one compute tint pass and one graphics list. Query allocation uses actual graph shape; arbitrary multi-queue execution remains a subsequent integration task.",
    "Current GPU constants use binary32 world positions/matrices. CPU camera construction validates representability, and the renderer separately validates the camera origin conversion. Camera-relative large-world rendering retains its later implementation status.",
    "This review did not perform independent interactive GPU capture. The r3 CPU regression was executed; GPU validation and dynamic image evidence are owned by /root/m42_network_acceptance.",
    "After the r3 observations, the RenderConfiguration source/header/schema/test files and VisualRuntime/Deferred shader files were normalized from CRLF to LF. Current input SHA-256 values above bind the normalized files. The r3 build report binds their earlier exact bytes, and the post-review normalization list records both values.",
